FongMi/FFmpeg (branch release-9.1-fongmi): fall back to the Dolby Vision
base layer when the sink demands native DV but the device has no DV decoder.

Problem: with vo=mediacodec_embed, mpv sets the decoder AVOption
dovi_sink_support=1 from the VO's VO_CAP_NATIVE_DOVI capability, so
mediacodec_decode_init() unconditionally requests a native Dolby Vision
MediaCodec decoder for DV streams. On devices without one (e.g. a
HDR10/HLG-only phone), ff_mediacodec_dec_init() fails in
getCodecNameByType(video/dolby-vision, ...) and playback ends with
audio only ("Video: no video"), even for Profile 8.1 streams whose
HDR10 base layer the device decodes fine - the same streams play
correctly through a non-embed output, where dovi_sink_support=0 takes
the existing base-layer fallback.

Fix: when a native DV decoder was requested and the stream has a
compatible base layer, probe MediaCodecList once for a DV decoder of
the stream's profile; if none exists, clear decoder_dovi so the
existing base-layer path runs. Devices with a DV decoder are
unaffected, and profiles without a compatible base layer (e.g. 5)
still fail as before.

Apply in the FFmpeg tree:  git apply ffmpeg-dovi-base-layer-fallback.patch
(or: patch -p1 < ffmpeg-dovi-base-layer-fallback.patch)

--- a/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodecdec.c
@@ -777,6 +777,26 @@
         decoder_dovi = NULL;
     }
 
+    /* A sink can declare native Dolby Vision support (the embedded
+     * MediaCodec output does) on a device that has no Dolby Vision
+     * decoder at all. Demanding one then fails outright even when the
+     * stream's base layer is fully compatible, so probe for the decoder
+     * first and fall back to the base layer when it is missing. */
+    if (decoder_dovi &&
+        mediacodec_dovi_has_compatible_base_layer(avctx, decoder_dovi)) {
+        char *dv_codec_name = ff_AMediaCodecList_getCodecNameByType(
+            FF_MEDIACODEC_MIME_DOLBY_VISION, 1 << decoder_dovi->dv_profile,
+            0, NULL, avctx);
+        if (!dv_codec_name) {
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING,
+                   "No Dolby Vision MediaCodec decoder for profile %u, "
+                   "using the base-layer decoder\n",
+                   decoder_dovi->dv_profile);
+            decoder_dovi = NULL;
+        }
+        av_freep(&dv_codec_name);
+    }
+
     ret = mediacodec_init_decoder(avctx, s, decoder_dovi);
     if (ret < 0)
         goto fail;
